# ── Repo-specific ──
## Large build artifacts - keep folders via .gitkeep
libs/**
libs/*
libs/
## EXCEPTION: 1_workflows/src/libs/ is engine source code, NOT build artifacts.
## Same convention as the cloud repo. Added 2026-05-16 after the engine broke
## because inject-header.sh was ignored despite being referenced by build.sh.
!1_workflows/src/libs/
!1_workflows/src/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_superapp/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:mail, libs:cal, …). Each is its own Android library
## with build.gradle + src/. NOT build artifacts. Added 2026-05-29 when
## the scaffold landed and these files silently disappeared on git add.
!ea_superapp/libs/
!ea_superapp/libs/**
## Upstream tracking clones (workspace-only — never vendored).
## Pattern: ea_<domain>-<project>/ holds a shallow clone of the upstream
## FOSS app we're cherry-picking into ea_superapp/libs/<domain>/.
## Today: ea_mail-fairmail (FairEmail, GPLv3), ea_cal-davx5 (DAVx5, GPLv3),
## ea_feed-feeder (Feeder, GPLv3), ea_net-wireguard (wireguard-android,
## Apache-2.0), ea_vault-keepassdx (KeePassDX, GPLv3). Each is refreshed
## with `git -C ea_<x>-<y> pull` independently. The single `-` in the
## directory name discriminates against `ea_superapp/` (no dash).
ea_*-*/
